# what the image build never takes: build output, deps (rebuilt inside), runtime data, secrets, history, private docs
node_modules
dist
data
global-memory
share
.git
.env
*.log
docs/plan
docs/archive
docs/agent/05_TODO.md
docs/agent/06_CHANGES.md
docs/hooks/.allow-*
# the install in the image is not a working repo: without its marker /app is no project of the daemon (the real zemory
# repo is seen through the workspace mount, as natively) - measured 2026-10-22: /app showed up as an extra repo "app"
docs/.harness.json
docs_visual
# HS and the sets are read from the clone mounted at /host/zemory (ZEMORY_SELF, plan/30 §3i), never from the image; and
# the attic is 1.2 GB of history. Sent over the Windows-drive mount they made the build context fail with "cannot
# allocate memory" (measured 2026-10-22). Only the legacy templates `adopt` reads stay.
docs_template
attic
!attic/legacy-templates
